# Met Pomodoro — project rules

macOS desktop overlay pomodoro timer. Breaks **paint** a bundled Met Open Access (CC0) artwork; the next study session dissolves it over 30s (click-through).

Repo name is historical (`moma-pomodoro`). **Art source is The Met, not MoMA.** No runtime image fetch — everything lives in `public/artworks/`.

## Stack

- **Tauri 2** — native window (always-on-top, frameless, fullscreen, click-through)
- **React + TypeScript + Vite** — UI
- **Canvas 2D** — construct / dissolve painting in `src/art/painter.ts`
- **Pure TS engine** — `src/engine/pomodoro.ts` + Vitest

## Module boundaries

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/shared/` | Frozen contract (`types.ts`, `events.ts`). Change only with care. |
| `src/app/App.tsx` | Composition root — wires engine, window, painter, UI. |
| `src/app/windowBridge.ts` | Window modes: `idle`, `compact`, `fullscreen`, `dissolve`. |
| `src/engine/` | Pomodoro state machine. No imports from Tauri, window, or canvas. |
| `src/art/` | Catalog, stroke extraction, canvas painter. |
| `src/ui/` | Settings, study chip, break-complete, back-to-work. |
| `src-tauri/` | Rust shell and Tauri config. |

Specialists must not import each other's internals. Public types flow through `src/shared/`.

## Shared contract (do not drift)

- Phases: `idle | studying | break | breakComplete | dissolving`
- `TimerConfig`: `{ studySeconds, breakSeconds }` (whole seconds)
- `DISSOLVE_MS = 30_000`
- Engine callbacks: **`onTick` and `onPhaseChange` only**
- `Artwork.description` is required — a fun personal-history fact shown on break-complete

## Painting behavior

- Construct runs over the **break duration**; each stroke should **reveal** the real bundled image (mask + wet paint that dries), not swap strokes for a full-image pop at the end.
- Break-complete shows the faithful source image plus title, artist, year, description.
- Dissolve fades the completed painting during the first 30s of the next study session.

## Art catalog

- CC0 / Public Domain Open Access only ([Met Open Access](https://metmuseum.github.io/))
- JSON catalog: `public/artworks/artworks.json` matching `Artwork` in `src/shared/types.ts`
- Credit: `"The Metropolitan Museum of Art, Open Access (CC0)"` plus collection credit

## When editing

- Match existing naming, types, and file layout. Minimal diffs.
- Run `node ./node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit` and `npm test` before finishing.
- Do not commit unless the user asks.
